> Allocation follows usage, with stable ties

At empty usage, the first slot receives almost all allocation. The source epsilon maps usage to1e-6+(1-1e-6)u; stable ranks stop derivatives while sorted usage values retain them. An untied row exposes all four soft allocation values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dnc_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto values=n::concat({m::DncAllocation(n::zeros({1,4})),m::DncAllocation(n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{.8f,.1f,.6f,.3f},{1,4}))},0).reshape({8});if(values.to_vector<float>()[0]<.99999)return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/dnc_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("Allocation follows usage, with stable ties").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/dnc_worked.svg");}
