> Trace an executed native operation

The block graph is traced from the actual operation below. Named stages mark its semantic endpoints; the complete program supplies the source geometry and parameter census.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dnc_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(45203);auto lengths=n::from_vector(std::vector<int>{2});n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto y=m::DncSequence(p,x,lengths);n::model_stage("LSTM8 controller",x,y.at("h"));n::model_stage("Four-slot allocation",y.at("h"),y.at("allocation"));return n::model_stage("Copy logits:3",y.at("allocation"),y.at("logits"));},"dnc: native operation");n::ModelPlotOptions o;o.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;o.sizing.minimum_extent=2;o.sizing.max_planes=2;model.plot(n::zeros({1,9,4}),o).save_svg("build/dnc_network.svg");}
