> Interpretation

Use the computed checks, held-out tables and galleries to assess this bounded run. Exact enumeration is restricted to tiny binary models; CD is a stopped sampled surrogate, and ULA is discretized sampling. The attention and memory fixtures verify mechanisms, not natural-language or long-memory benchmarks. Weak results remain part of the report.

> Count every held-out recall bit

Only recall steps contribute. This matrix uses current saved test logits and targets; it is distinct from whole-sequence exact-copy success.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dnc_confusion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> output,data;for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/generative-models/models/dnc/outputs.npz"))output.emplace(key,value);for(auto& [key,value]:n::load_npz("build/generative-models/models/dnc/data.npz"))data.emplace(key,value);std::vector<n::Tensor> targets,predictions;auto lengths=data.at("test_lengths").to_vector<std::int32_t>();for(std::size_t row=0;row<lengths.size();++row){auto start=lengths[row]+1,end=2*lengths[row]+1;targets.push_back(n::reshape(n::cast(n::greater(n::slice_axis(n::select(data.at("test_target"),0,row),0,start,end),0.),n::DType::Int64),{-1}));predictions.push_back(n::reshape(n::cast(n::greater(n::slice_axis(n::select(output.at("logits"),0,row),0,start,end),0.),n::DType::Int64),{-1}));}auto truth=n::concat(targets,0),pred=n::concat(predictions,0); n::ConfusionMatrix cm(2);cm.add(truth,pred);cm.save_svg("build/dnc_confusion.svg",{.title="Differentiable Neural Computer: held-out confusion"});n::save_npz("build/dnc_confusion.npz",{{"counts",cm.to_tensor()}});std::cout<<"Truth rows, prediction columns; "<<truth.numel()<<" held-out observations\n";for(const auto& row:cm.cells()){for(auto count:row)std::cout<<count<<" ";std::cout<<"\n";}}

